<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander Dubček</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1921–1992</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander Dubček was a Slovak politician who became first secretary of the Communist Party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> in January 1968. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague-spring">Prague Spring</a> reforms, promising 'socialism with a human face', eased censorship and encouraged open debate until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw-pact">Warsaw Pact</a> invasion of August 1968 ended them. Removed in 1969, he returned after the Velvet Revolution as chairman of the federal parliament.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-dubcek.jpg" alt="Alexander Dubček" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CTK · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Alexander_Dubcek_in_August_23rd,_1968_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
